* Modular commutation-capacitance assembly for the P24_TABLE3_CANDIDATE branch.
* STATUS: candidate only. Not included by any active/graded netlist as of
* 2026-09-14. Do not wire this into R04D*/A37-A44 netlists without opening a
* new, separately-numbered experiment; those results are graded against the
* GS61008T-based GS61008T_commutation_capacitance.lib and must not be
* silently changed underneath them.
* Device Coss source: EPC2067 datasheet, revised 2021-10-21 (external device data).
* Population source: 2024 Table 3, nP=4/nM=4 row (2 parallel high-side,
* 3 parallel low-side EPC2067) -- re-verified 2026-09-15 directly against
* the printed table (HS/LS peak-current formula values 125 A/200 A match
* the row exactly) and cross-checked against Table 3's own nM=8 row, which
* the paper's body text separately describes in words ("a single EPC2067...
* two parallel switches") and which matches that row's 1 HS/2 LS reading.
* Note: nM=4 (used here, matching this project's 250 W/module mainline) is
* a correctly-read row of the same table, but is NOT the row Sec. IV's own
* headline package-integration example (Fig. 5, the conclusion's size
* estimate) uses -- that example is nM=8, not nM=4.
* This is 2024's own Sec. IV embedded/3-D package integration selection,
* NOT confirmed to be the device the Sec. II-B ZVS mechanism itself
* assumes -- see SOURCE_COVERAGE_MATRIX.md.
* External snubber values are not published by P24/P25 and default to zero.
* Control thresholds and timing must be defined outside this component module.
.param NHS=2 NLS=3
.param CH_DEVICE={NHS*EPC2067_COTR_0_20V}
.param CL_DEVICE={NLS*EPC2067_COTR_0_20V}
.param CH_SNUBBER=0
.param CL_SNUBBER=0
.param CH_TOTAL={CH_DEVICE+CH_SNUBBER}
.param CL_TOTAL={CL_DEVICE+CL_SNUBBER}
